1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,750
Good morning.

2
00:00:01,750 --> 00:00:03,539
Oh, good morning.

3
00:00:03,539 --> 00:00:05,078
Is this...

4
00:00:05,078 --> 00:00:05,743
er...

5
00:00:05,743 --> 00:00:07,740
room number 26?

6
00:00:07,740 --> 00:00:07,790
Yes,

7
00:00:07,790 --> 00:00:08,770
that's right.

8
00:00:08,770 --> 00:00:11,800
So is this the Student Job Centre?

9
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:12,700
It certainly is.

10
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:14,200
How can I help you?

11
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:18,276
Well, actually I'm looking for a job-a part-time job.

12
00:00:18,276 --> 00:00:21,900
Do you have anything available at the moment?

13
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:22,698
Ah, yes...

14
00:00:22,698 --> 00:00:24,692
Are you a registered student?

15
00:00:24,692 --> 00:00:28,680
I'm afraid this service is only available to full-time students.

16
00:00:28,680 --> 00:00:29,048
Yes...

17
00:00:29,048 --> 00:00:29,784
I am.

18
00:00:29,784 --> 00:00:32,359
I'm doing a degree in Business Studies.

19
00:00:32,359 --> 00:00:33,830
Here's my student card.

20
00:00:33,830 --> 00:00:36,300
Which year are you in?

21
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:36,632
Well...

22
00:00:36,632 --> 00:00:40,955
I've been at university for four years but I'm in the Third Year

23
00:00:40,955 --> 00:00:42,950
because I took last year off.

24
00:00:42,950 --> 00:00:43,322
Right...

25
00:00:43,322 --> 00:00:48,529
well, let's just have a look at what positions are available at the moment.

26
00:00:48,529 --> 00:00:55,596
There's a job working at the reception desk at the Sports Centre, for three evenings a week-that's Wednesdays, Thursdays

27
00:00:55,596 --> 00:00:56,340
and Fridays.

28
00:00:56,340 --> 00:01:02,807
That sounds like fun but unfortunately I have evening lectures-so that's not possible, I'm

29
00:01:02,807 --> 00:01:03,269
afraid.

30
00:01:03,269 --> 00:01:06,040
Is there anything during the day?

31
00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:06,498
OK,

32
00:01:06,498 --> 00:01:08,330
that's no good then.

33
00:01:08,330 --> 00:01:08,788
Um.

34
00:01:08,788 --> 00:01:10,162
What about cleaning?

35
00:01:10,162 --> 00:01:15,200
There's a position for a cleaner at the Child Care Centre.

36
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:16,310
Right...

37
00:01:16,310 --> 00:01:18,928
But you'd need to be there at 6 am.

38
00:01:18,928 --> 00:01:19,800
Does that appeal?

39
00:01:19,800 --> 00:01:21,474
Six o'clock in the morning!

40
00:01:21,474 --> 00:01:21,809
Oh,

41
00:01:21,809 --> 00:01:24,487
that's far too early for me, I'm afraid.

42
00:01:24,487 --> 00:01:27,500
I'd never make it that early in the morning.

43
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:27,900
Mmm...

44
00:01:27,900 --> 00:01:31,496
Well-there was a position going in the Computer Lab.

45
00:01:31,496 --> 00:01:35,093
for three days a week that might be OK.

46
00:01:35,093 --> 00:01:36,692
Ah, here it is!

47
00:01:36,692 --> 00:01:42,287
No, it's in the Library, not the Lab., Clerical Assistant required-I think it mostly

48
00:01:42,287 --> 00:01:45,484
involves putting the books back on the shelves.

49
00:01:45,484 --> 00:01:46,683
Oh no-hang on.

50
00:01:46,683 --> 00:01:49,480
It's for Wednesday and Friday evenings again.

51
00:01:49,480 --> 00:01:52,050
NO-I can't manage that because of the lectures.

52
00:01:52,050 --> 00:01:53,898
OK, I'm getting the idea.

53
00:01:53,898 --> 00:01:57,595
Look, I'll just get a few details from you anyway,

54
00:01:57,595 --> 00:02:02,400
and then we can check through the list and see what comes up.

55
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:09,150
We'll fill in the personal details on this application form first, if that's OK?

56
00:02:09,150 --> 00:02:09,543
Yes,

57
00:02:09,543 --> 00:02:10,330
that's fine.

58
00:02:10,330 --> 00:02:12,000
Now, what's your name again?

59
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:16,940
Anita Newman-that's N-E-W-M-A-N.

60
00:02:16,940 --> 00:02:18,600
And your address, Anita?

61
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:23,397
I'm in one of the Halls of Residence for post-graduate students, you know, International

62
00:02:23,397 --> 00:02:23,740
House.

63
00:02:23,740 --> 00:02:24,571
OK-that's easy.

64
00:02:24,571 --> 00:02:26,650
What's your room number there?

65
00:02:26,650 --> 00:02:29,247
Room B569 - no sorry B659.

66
00:02:29,247 --> 00:02:31,844
I always get that wrong.

67
00:02:31,844 --> 00:02:35,480
I haven't been living there very long.

68
00:02:35,480 --> 00:02:37,165
Do you have any other skills?

69
00:02:37,165 --> 00:02:37,727
Typing, languages,

70
00:02:37,727 --> 00:02:38,850
that sort of thing?

71
00:02:38,850 --> 00:02:41,160
Well, I speak some Japanese.

72
00:02:41,160 --> 00:02:43,983
Right, I'll make a note of that.

73
00:02:43,983 --> 00:02:46,403
Now-let's see what else is available.

74
00:02:46,403 --> 00:02:49,227
What do you think of administrative work?

75
00:02:49,227 --> 00:02:54,470
There is a position for an Office Assistant at the English Language Centre.

76
00:02:54,470 --> 00:02:56,420
That sounds interesting.

77
00:02:56,420 --> 00:03:01,129
It's for 3 days a week-Monday, Friday and Saturday mornings.

78
00:03:01,129 --> 00:03:01,600
Interested?

79
00:03:01,600 --> 00:03:02,032
Mmm.

80
00:03:02,032 --> 00:03:05,058
I was hoping to have Saturdays free.

81
00:03:05,058 --> 00:03:07,652
But I need the work so ...

82
00:03:07,652 --> 00:03:11,110
can you tell me what the job involves?

83
00:03:11,110 --> 00:03:11,720
Yes, sure.

84
00:03:11,720 --> 00:03:15,380
It says here that you'll be required to deal with student enquiries

85
00:03:15,380 --> 00:03:16,600
and answer the phone.

86
00:03:16,600 --> 00:03:19,440
I'm sure I can handle all that without a problem.

87
00:03:19,440 --> 00:03:19,782
Great.

88
00:03:19,782 --> 00:03:23,541
Well, would you like me to arrange an interview for you?

89
00:03:23,541 --> 00:03:25,250
Say, Friday morning, around ten?

90
00:03:25,250 --> 00:03:27,549
Could we make it a bit later?

91
00:03:27,549 --> 00:03:30,176
Unfortunately, I've got something to do at ten.

92
00:03:30,176 --> 00:03:31,490
Would that be OK?

93
00:03:31,490 --> 00:03:32,585
Not a problem.

94
00:03:32,585 --> 00:03:34,045
How about eleven thirty?

95
00:03:34,045 --> 00:03:36,600
Hope it works out for you Anita.

96
00:03:36,600 --> 00:03:37,138
Me too.

97
00:03:37,138 --> 00:03:38,750
And thanks for all your help.
